__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.db
usage.db
projects.db
compacts/
knowledge_uploads/
node_modules/
.venv/
venv/
scratch/
companion/dist/
config/providers.json
config/providers.json.migrated
config/providers/
# NOTE: /.agents was previously listed here while 69 of its files were still tracked, which
# made the rule a no-op and hid the real state. It stays tracked on purpose: 8 installed
# skills (code-review, commit-style, docx, frontend-design, goal, grill-me, pdf, web-research)
# exist ONLY here and are not in skill_catalog/, so untracking it would drop them from every
# fresh clone. The duplicates that ARE safe to drop - .claude/skills, a byte-identical copy of
# .agents/skills - are removed instead.
# Agent-tool worktrees and state. These were only excluded via .git/info/exclude, which is a
# LOCAL file that is never committed - so a fresh clone showed a whole duplicate tree as
# untracked, including a stale 100 KB server_manager.py.bak.
/.kilo/
/.kilocode/
/.claude/worktrees/
/.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
/.claude/scheduled_tasks.json
/.claude/routines/.state/
/.claude/checkpoints/
/.claude/mailbox/
# Installed copies, not sources. plugin_catalog/ is the tracked, reviewed set; the Customize
# page copies a folder into plugins/ to activate it (core/plugins/catalog.py) and load_plugins()
# already tolerates the directory being absent. Tracking the copies made a local edit
# indistinguishable from an install in a diff - all 10 files were byte-identical to the catalog.
/plugins/
# Schema-repair snapshots (core/db_repair.py). Trimmed to DB_BACKUP_KEEP newest on each backup;
# they are a safety net for a botched migration, not an archive.
db_backups/
# coverage.py's binary SQLite report. A 975 KB machine-local snapshot of one developer's run,
# rewritten by every `coverage run` (pyproject ratchets fail_under off it), which is why the
# working tree was permanently dirty. Regenerate with `coverage run -m unittest discover tests`.
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
# NOTE: tests/.eval_vec_cache.json is deliberately NOT ignored. It looks like a build artifact
# but tests/test_knowledge_recall.py asserts it exists and matches the current chunk params, and
# CI never regenerates it - scripts/embed_eval_corpus.py needs a local embedder on :8093. It is a
# golden fixture, like tests/eval_baseline.json.
# llama-server daily logs (core/state.py). Machine-local diagnostics, rotated by LOG_KEEP_DAYS.
/logs/
# The 737 KB PNG is a manual screenshot of the SVG next to it (see
# diagram/gen_system_architecture.py, which writes the SVG). The SVG is the source of truth.
diagram/*.png
# companion runtime config (server URL) - keep out of git
companion/.env
# SQLite sidecars can hold recent rows (sessions, chat text) just like the .db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.db-journal
*.bak
